# Snippet render safety (Svelte 5)

Rendering `null`/`undefined` snippets throws [`invalid_snippet`](https://svelte.dev/e/invalid_snippet) and can break navigation (uncaught promise, “stuck loading”).

## Optional snippets (default)

- Type slot props as `children?: Snippet` (import `type { Snippet } from 'svelte'`), not `() => void`.
- Render with a guard:

```svelte
{#if children}
	{@render children()}
{/if}
```

Do **not** use `{@render children()}` or `{@render children?.()}` when the snippet may be omitted.

## Required snippets

When the API always provides the snippet, type `name: Snippet` and `{@render name()}` is allowed without a guard.

## Wash / slot adapters

Components that wrap default slot content (`WashCard`, `WashCardBody`, `WashCardBodyTitle`, layouts, etc.) treat `children` as **optional** unless documented otherwise.

Do not pass ad-hoc props (`title`, `subtitle`) to Wash adapters unless that component defines them — put copy in the default slot / `children`.

## Local `#snippet` in the same file

Calls like `{@render mySection()}` for a `#snippet mySection()` defined in the same file do not need `{#if}` (the snippet exists). Still guard props typed `foo?: Snippet`.

## CI

`pnpm run check:snippet-render` enforces guards for optional snippets and bare `children` renders.